  "note": "Extracted by hand from the ordering schematic, the model printed as spaced characters in the head and the numbered positions assembled bare after it. The orifice number follows a dash, the dimension tables' own part numbers printing the form, while the schematic example row spaces the digits without one, held for John. The orifice ladder is held to the sheet's per size table, dual pressure rows folded. The size ladder prints 5 twice, at 1-1/4 and again at 1-1/2 inch, so the first printing is carried, the union of both rows' orifices allowed, and choosing 5 raises a caution.",
  "assembly": "{model}{size}{connections}-{orifice}",
